## 2. Functional M’MOFs for Gas Storage and Separation
Our group is now focused on the construction of microporous M’MOFs with rationally immobilized open metal sites for gas storage and separation.[10,11] We have shown that in the first step, a ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{\mathrm{{II}}}$ Schiff base complex in the form of the metalloligand building block $\{\mathrm{Cu(Pyen)}\}$ could be readily achieved via the condensation of corresponding aldehyde and ethylenediamine and further complexation with $\mathrm{Cu}(\mathsf{N O}_{3})_{2}$ .[10] This metallo-Schiff base contains two free terminal pyridine moieties available for binding with other metal ions for the second step reaction (Figure 1 I a). A solvothermal reaction among $\mathrm{[Cu(H_{2}P y e n)](N O_{3})_{2}}$ , benzene-1,4-dicarboxylic acid $\left(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{bdc}\right)$ , and $Z_{\mathrm{{n}}}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}$ led to the formation of $[Z\mathrm{n}_{3}(\mathrm{bdc})_{3}\mathrm{Cu}-$ $\mathrm{(Pyen)(G)_{\mathrm{x}}]}$ (M’MOF 1; $\mathbf{G}=$ guest molecules). The framework is composed of trinuclear $\{Z{\bf n}_{3}(\mathrm{COO})_{6}\}$ SBUs (Figure 1I b). These SBUs are bridged by bdc moieties to form $3^{6}$ tessellated $\{Z{\bmod{\mathrm{c}}}\}$ 2D sheets (Figure 1 I c) that are further pillared by the $\{\mathrm{Cu(Pyen)}\}$ units to build the 3D network. The rationally immobilized Cu centers reside within two types of micropores (curved pores and irregular ultra-micropores along $c$ and $b$ directions, respectively; Figure 1 I d,e), which interact with $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ molecules through two open metal sites per copper atom with an enthalpy of $(12.29\pm0.53)\mathrm{kJmol^{-1}}$ at zero coverage (Figure 1 II). The most significant feature was the differential adsorption kinetics for $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and ${\bf D}_{2}$ (Figure 1III). The rate constant for ${\bf D}_{2}$ was higher but the activation energy was slightly lower compared to the corresponding values for $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ . The higher effective collision crosssection of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ , because of